ion":[{"accession":"O75976","text":"Functions in the processing of proteins and peptides in the secretory pathway. Mechanistically, cleaves exclusively C-terminal basic residues. By removing terminal residues, can modulate the activity, stability, and receptor-binding properties of bioactive peptides. (Microbial infection) Acts as an alternative entry receptor for adeno-associated virus (AAV)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}